{
 "title": "LIF with an adaptive threshold",
 "description": "A leaky integrate-and-fire layer whose threshold rises each time it fires and decays back: a third state a = ρ·a_prev + s_prev (ρ = 0.95) is added to the threshold, s = Spike(v − θ − b·a) with b = 0.2, so a neuron that has just fired is harder to fire again and its firing slows under steady input. Three Delays: v, s and a. 1,024 parameters.",
